cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "LeanCert: verified numerical computation for Lean 4"
authors:
  - family-names: "Radisic"
    given-names: "Alejandro"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-7612-1082"
repository-code: "https://github.com/alerad/leancert"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "4.33.0"
date-released: "2026-08-10"
abstract: >-
  LeanCert is a Lean 4 library for verified numerical computation:
  interval arithmetic, Taylor models, and certificate checkers that turn
  untrusted numerical candidates into kernel-checked bounds. Releases are
  pinned against matching Mathlib versions. It is the Lean core underlying
  the LeanCert Python SDK.
keywords:
  - "Lean 4"
  - "formal verification"
  - "interval arithmetic"
  - "Taylor models"
  - "verified numerics"
  - "certificates"
